From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:13:57 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 74/77] Meridian: profiles per space the Arc way, one window
 for every profile
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A window holds the tabs of every space, each made in its space's profile
(links in their page's), so switching spaces never changes windows. The
tabs' profiles survive session restore, Chrome's session rebuilds and
⇧⌘T; the windows left by the old one-window-per-profile model are
gathered into one, once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
